WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
Movie scaling the DNA

00:05.140 --> 00:10.040
Hi, I'm Zoe and I'm super duper curious about everything

00:10.920 --> 00:17.060
Especially teeny tiny things. We can't see um like you know the stuff inside us that makes us us

00:18.360 --> 00:24.820
Today in science class miss helix was talking about something called DNA. It sounded really confusing and kind of boring

00:24.820 --> 00:26.820
But

00:29.260 --> 00:35.500
Then the craziest thing happened I started shrinking everything around me got bigger and bigger whoa

00:35.860 --> 00:43.540
Where am I everything looks so blobby and weird? Hey there little Explorer. I'm Danny a DNA strand

00:43.860 --> 00:50.020
Welcome to the inside of a cell your DNA, but you're so big and colorful. I thought DNA was tiny

00:50.300 --> 00:53.420
Well you shrunk down to see me want to learn what I do

00:53.700 --> 00:59.620
Yes, please. This is way more fun than science class great hop on and let's take a ride through the cell

01:05.940 --> 01:08.660
We this is amazing, so what do you do Danny?

01:08.660 --> 01:14.140
I'm like a big book of instructions for your body. I tell your cells how to make you well you wow

01:14.300 --> 01:18.500
So you're like a recipe for me exactly and I made up of four special ingredients

01:19.180 --> 01:21.960
A T C and G like alphabet soup

01:22.600 --> 01:29.120
Kind of but instead of spelling words we spell out instructions for your body. That's so cool. What kind of instructions?

01:37.160 --> 01:43.140
Well I might say make blue eyes or grow curly hair or even be good at math no way you decide all that

01:43.280 --> 01:45.280
Yep, and now watch this cool trick

01:45.280 --> 01:47.280
Oh

01:50.280 --> 01:52.240
Whoa you're splitting in half

01:52.240 --> 01:58.320
Yep, it's called replication. I make copies of myself so new cells can grow that's so cool

01:58.320 --> 02:02.040
You're like a superhero of the cell. Thanks Zoe remember

02:02.040 --> 02:07.440
You're made of billions of cells each with its own DNA pretty amazing, huh? It sure is

02:07.440 --> 02:10.140
I can't wait to tell everyone about you Danny oh

02:11.100 --> 02:13.100
Oh

02:14.060 --> 02:17.160
No, I think I'm starting to grow back to my normal size

02:17.500 --> 02:25.420
Bye Danny bye Zoe remember science is awesome now. I know that DNA isn't boring at all. It's the coolest thing ever

02:25.740 --> 02:31.140
It's what makes me me and guess what there's DNA in all living things

02:32.140 --> 02:35.020
plants animals even tiny bacteria

02:35.020 --> 02:41.840
So next time you look in the mirror remember you're looking at a walking talking DNA masterpiece

